<figure class="versions" aria-labelledby="r15-version-title" data-r15-versions>
 <figcaption id="r15-version-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Two readers, one product</figcaption>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="readers"><p>Report R<br /><strong data-report data-live>20.00</strong><small>Repeatable Read snapshot</small></p><p>New query Q<br /><strong data-query data-live>20.00</strong><small>Starts at this step</small></p></div>
  <div class="page"><p class="page-label">One heap page · illustrative layout</p><div class="version" data-old><b>P7</b><strong>20.00</strong><span data-old-state data-live>Current version</span></div><div class="version" data-new hidden><b>P7</b><strong>25.00</strong><span data-new-state data-live>Uncommitted version</span></div><div class="space" data-space hidden>Space available for reuse</div></div>
  <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">R takes a snapshot while P7 costs 20.00. Both readers can see that version.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Row version steps"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>All steps as text</summary><ol><li>R takes a Repeatable Read snapshot of P7 at 20.00.</li><li>A writer creates a 25.00 version but has not committed. R and another ordinary reader still get 20.00.</li><li>The writer commits. R still gets 20.00; a query taking a new snapshot gets 25.00.</li><li>Vacuum cannot reclaim 20.00 while R may need it.</li><li>R finishes. Its snapshot no longer retains the old version.</li><li>Cleanup makes the old version's space reusable. The page remains part of the file.</li></ol></details>
 <p class="caption">Chosen schedule, not a page capture. R is a read-only Repeatable Read transaction. Q takes a fresh snapshot each time. The model leaves out other rows, indexes and tuple headers.</p>
</figure>
<style>
figure{font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-family:var(--font-serif)}

.versions{margin:2rem 0}.versions figcaption{font-size:1.12rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}.versions figcaption span{font: .75rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:.6rem}.scene{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);background:var(--color-surface);padding:1rem}.readers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem}.readers p{margin:0 0 1rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.4rem}.readers strong{display:block;font-size:1.5rem}.readers small{display:block;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.75rem}.page{border:2px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.7rem;min-height:12rem}.page-label{font: .75rem var(--font-mono);margin:0 0 .7rem}.version{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.5rem 4rem 1fr;gap:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.7rem;margin:.5rem 0}.version[data-old][data-retained=true]{border-color:var(--color-accent)}.version[data-new][data-committed=true]{border-color:var(--color-accent)}.version span{font-size:.85rem}.space{border:1px dashed var(--color-rule);padding:.7rem;font-size:.85rem}.explanation{min-height:5rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem;margin:1rem 0 0}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-top:0}.controls button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.4rem .7rem;cursor:pointer}.controls button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.controls button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}.controls [data-step]{margin-left:auto;font: .8rem var(--font-mono);align-self:center}[data-hold]{flex-basis:100%;height:3px;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent);width:0}.caption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin:.8rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:450px){.scene{padding:.7rem}.version{grid-template-columns:2rem 3.3rem 1fr;padding:.6rem .4rem;gap:.35rem}.explanation{min-height:8rem}.readers small{font-size:.7rem}}
</style>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-r15-versions]').forEach(root=>{
 const qs=(s:string)=>root.querySelector(s) as HTMLElement;
 const explanations=[
 'R takes a snapshot while P7 costs 20.00. Both readers can see that version.',
 'The writer adds 25.00 but has not committed. Other readers still see 20.00; the writer can read its own change.',
 'The writer commits. R keeps reading 20.00. Q takes a new snapshot and reads 25.00. Commit did not erase the old version.',
 'Vacuum runs, but R can still need 20.00. That version must remain. A committed update is not permission to reclaim its predecessor.',
 'R ends its transaction. In this drawing no other snapshot needs 20.00, so it is now eligible for cleanup.',
 'Cleanup reclaims 20.00. Its space can hold a later version or another row. This page still belongs to the table file.'
 ];
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>explanations.length,draw(s:number){
  qs('[data-report]').textContent=s<4?'20.00':'Finished'; qs('[data-query]').textContent=s<2?'20.00':'25.00';
  qs('[data-old]').hidden=s===5;qs('[data-new]').hidden=s===0;qs('[data-space]').hidden=s!==5;
  qs('[data-old]').dataset.retained=String(s>=2&&s<4);qs('[data-new]').dataset.committed=String(s>=2);
  qs('[data-old-state]').textContent=s<2?'Visible to both readers':s<4?'Retained for R':'Eligible for cleanup';
  qs('[data-new-state]').textContent=s<2?'Writer only':'Visible to new snapshots';qs('[data-explanation]').textContent=explanations[s];
 }});
});
</script>
